E1 = 'Urban farming has expanded rapidly in many cities over the past decade. Rooftop gardens and vertical farms allow residents to grow vegetables close to where they live, reducing the distance food travels. Supporters argue that this lowers transport emissions and gives city dwellers fresher produce. Critics, however, point out that the high electricity cost of indoor lighting can cancel out these environmental gains. A recent study found that rooftop gardens using sunlight were far more energy-efficient than windowless vertical farms, though they produced smaller harvests.'
