E2 = 'Many schools ban smartphones during class hours, yet some teachers have started inviting students to use them as learning tools. In one classroom, students record short science experiments and share the videos with classmates, which teacher Ms. Lestari says makes lessons "stick." Still, she admits that managing the devices demands extra planning. "A phone can open a library or a game with the same tap," she says. She therefore sets clear rules: phones stay face down until she gives a signal.'
