E3 = 'The traditional batik of Java is made by drawing patterns with hot wax on cloth before the fabric is dyed. The wax resists the dye, so the covered areas keep their original color. Artisans may repeat this process several times to build up complex designs, which is why a single piece can take weeks to finish. In 2009, UNESCO recognized batik as part of humanity\'s intangible cultural heritage, a decision that helped raise global interest.'
